scope: |
  Give the v2 lane a real Char. `'x'` was the Int 120 in println/.toString/concatenation
  (`v2-char-is-an-int`) because the char literal became an INT TOKEN in both fronts' lexers.
  Shape (owner's call): both fronts lower `'x'` to `(prim char (lit (int 120)))` and the
  runtime gets `CharV extends IntV`. The frozen specs/12-ir-format.md is UNTOUCHED — a new
  prim, not a new Const kind — and the subclass keeps all 273 numeric IntV sites correct by
  construction instead of by enumeration.
  WIDENED 2026-07-31 from the original 7 paths: the three source generators (jvm/rust/js)
  each need the prim or they gain an `unknown prim1` on every char literal; the two frozen
  corpus files because ANY new conformance case fails the gate until the roster names it
  (measured: exit 1 even when all observed cells PASS); and the jvm module's BUGS.md for
  `jvm-string-literal-s-concat-inserts-x`, found while establishing this case's golden.
next: backends, e2e numeric-position gate, then the roster refresh on a quiet host
